  "summary": "I added Red, Blue and Black buttons in a row under the canvas, and `window.__TASK_STATE__` now includes `paintColor`. Typecheck passes and the render shows the buttons with no errors. I could not click the buttons in this environment, so the repaint itself has not been run.\n\n- **What each button does:** it changes only the base `color` of the body and roof-panel nodes, on both the car and its reflection. Red is `#70000f`, Blue is `#06208a` and Black is `#050506`.\n- **What stays the same:** the clear coat, the flake and normal maps, the chrome and the glass are untouched.\n- **State:** red is the starting colour. `paintColor` is `'red' | 'blue' | 'black'` and is written every frame next to `turntableAngleDeg` and `paintFinish`.\n- **Fallback if the repaint doesn't take:** if `setColor` is missing on a node, the code falls back to `setMaterial` with a copy of the paint material and the new colour. That fallback would also be untested.\n\nThe change is in `src/main.ts`."
